---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { appConfig, isConfiguredEmail } from '../config/app';
const privacyContactReady = isConfiguredEmail(appConfig.privacyEmail);
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | HealthWallet" description="Read how the HealthWallet mobile app handles account, health, location, and other information.">
  <div class="inner-hero"><div class="container"><span class="section-kicker">Your information</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>How HealthWallet handles information used by the mobile app and this website.</p></div></div>
  <div class="container content-wrap">
    <div class="legal-meta"><span>Effective date: {appConfig.privacyEffectiveDate}</span><span>Operator: {appConfig.developerName}</span></div>
    <aside class="notice"><strong>Publication details still required</strong>The legal operator, privacy contact, effective date, precise retention rules, children's age policy, and international transfer arrangements need review and configuration before this page is submitted to an app store. This policy describes behavior found in the application code; deployment and provider contracts must be checked separately.</aside>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>1. Scope and who uses the app</h2><p>HealthWallet is a mobile app for patients and members, and for participating doctors, coaches, and administrators. It helps users keep health information, connect with providers, find nearby care, request appointments, and use fitness tools. This policy covers the app and this informational website. The operator is {appConfig.developerName}, at {appConfig.postalAddress}, {appConfig.country}.</p><p>HealthWallet is an information organizer and directory. It does not diagnose conditions, replace professional advice, or provide emergency care.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>2. Information handled by the mobile app</h2><ul>
      <li><strong>Account and contact details:</strong> phone number for one-time code sign-in; name, username, email or synthetic authentication address, address, and staff login credentials where applicable. Verification codes are delivered through WhatsApp or SMS. Authentication and session identifiers are also processed.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile and health details:</strong> date of birth, gender, blood type, emergency contact, conditions, symptoms, allergies, medications, surgeries, medical history, lifestyle answers, body measurements, and information you add to your profile.</li>
      <li><strong>Files and content:</strong> profile photos, medical document and receipt images, text recognized from documents, progress photos, private chat messages and images, and appointment notes.</li>
      <li><strong>Care and activity:</strong> appointments, linked doctors or coaches, workout and nutrition plans, fitness or water entries, in-app notifications, reports, blocks, and related moderation records.</li>
      <li><strong>Location:</strong> device location when you use nearby map or navigation features and grant permission. When you request a route, route coordinates are sent to the public OSRM routing service. Map tile requests also disclose the map area and ordinary network information to the tile service.</li>
      <li><strong>Payments:</strong> on Android, the app can offer FIB payments for access plans. The app handles the plan, expected amount and currency, payment identifier, status, and entitlement dates. Banking credentials are entered with FIB and are not received by the app. The current iOS build does not show a purchase flow.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> network request data and service security information. Google ML Kit may process device, app, feature-use, performance, and diagnostic information according to its SDK disclosures. Google Fonts may receive a request when a font is not bundled or cached.</li>
    </ul><p>The reviewed app code does not contain an advertising SDK or a separate app analytics or crash-reporting SDK. The in-app notification bell reads notifications stored in the app backend; a push notification SDK was not found in the reviewed dependencies.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>3. Why information is used</h2><p>Information is used to create and secure accounts, verify phone numbers, provide profiles and records, generate QR and PDF sharing selected by users, store documents, connect patients with care providers, handle appointments and chat, show maps and routes, support coaching features, process and verify Android payments, prevent abuse, and respond to support or safety reports. No sale of personal or health information or targeted advertising flow was found in the reviewed implementation.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>4. Camera, photos, files, and text recognition</h2><p>The app requests camera access for QR scanning and for taking profile or document photos. It can also let users choose images from their photo library for profile, document, progress, or chat content. Document text recognition uses Google ML Kit on the device; documents chosen for upload and recognized text can then be stored with the account. You can deny or revoke permissions in device settings, although related features may not work.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>5. Sharing and recipients</h2><p>Information is shared through features you use: showing a QR code, exporting a PDF, requesting an appointment, linking a doctor or coach, or participating in private chat. Linked providers may see information their app role and connection permit. Chat participants see messages in their conversation. Authorized administrators may perform directory, support, or safety functions. Service providers receive the information needed to deliver their services. Information may also be disclosed where required by applicable law.</p><p>The reviewed implementation uses these outside services:</p><ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase:</strong> authentication, PostgreSQL database, Edge Functions, and private file Storage. The linked project was documented as hosted in Tokyo, Japan; confirm the production project and region before publication.</li>
      <li><strong>OTPIQ:</strong> phone code delivery by WhatsApp or SMS.</li>
      <li><strong>FIB:</strong> Android payment creation and payment status verification.</li>
      <li><strong>OpenStreetMap tiles and public OSRM:</strong> maps and requested routes.</li>
      <li><strong>Google ML Kit and Google Fonts:</strong> on-device text recognition support and font delivery, including SDK or network data described above.</li>
    </ul></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>6. Storage, security, and international processing</h2><p>Application records and uploaded files are stored through Supabase. The code uses database row-level access policies, authenticated functions, short-lived file links, HTTPS requests, and secure operating-system storage for mobile authentication material. These safeguards reduce risk, but no online service can guarantee absolute security. Data may be processed outside Iraq, including at the documented Supabase project location in Japan. The operator must confirm current processing countries, provider agreements, and applicable transfer safeguards before publication.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2><p>Account information and content are used while an account is active and as needed to provide the service. The repository includes an in-app deletion action at <strong>Settings → Account → Delete account</strong> and a server function designed to remove user-owned stored files, then the authentication account and linked database records. The production deployment and end-to-end result need confirmation. See the <a href="/account-deletion">account deletion instructions</a> for the current process and request channel.</p><p><strong>Retention details to finalize:</strong> [RETENTION PERIODS], [PAYMENT OR LEGAL RECORD EXCEPTIONS], [BACKUP DELETION TIMING], [REPORT OR SAFETY RECORD RETENTION], and [PROCESSOR DELETION TIMING]. These are not established by the mobile source code and should be filled in after legal and operational review.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2><p>You can view and edit many profile and health fields in the app, decide whether to add optional information, choose whether to share through QR, PDF, links, and chat, and turn off camera, photo, or location access in device settings. You can start account deletion in the app. For access, correction, deletion, or other rights available under applicable law, contact {privacyContactReady ? <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.privacyEmail}`}>{appConfig.privacyEmail}</a> : <strong>{appConfig.privacyEmail}</strong>}.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>9. Children</h2><p>The final minimum age and parental consent rules have not been established from the implementation. <strong>[MINIMUM AGE AND PARENTAL CONSENT POLICY REQUIRED]</strong>. A parent or guardian with a concern should contact the privacy address above.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>10. This website</h2><p>This static website has no account system, contact form, advertising script, or site analytics in its source. It serves pages and images. Its eventual hosting provider may process ordinary request data such as an IP address and browser details; identify the provider and its retention practice before publication. Following a store link takes you to that store, which has its own privacy practices.</p></section>

    <section class="legal-section"><h2>11. Changes and contact</h2><p>When this policy changes, the effective date above should be updated. Significant changes should also be communicated through an appropriate app or support channel. Privacy questions may be sent to {privacyContactReady ? <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.privacyEmail}`}>{appConfig.privacyEmail}</a> : <strong>{appConfig.privacyEmail}</strong>}. Postal address: {appConfig.postalAddress}, {appConfig.country}.</p></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
